//- The select half of the pair: a portfolio, where the URL parameter decides
//- which work is shown.
//-
//- Every chapter has both a `data-name` and a `data-tag`, because that is
//- what this way round asks for — a parameter can only choose between sections
//- it can recognise. The two that must survive every parameter, the title and
//- "About this demo", have `data-tag="keep"` instead.

section.center(data-tag="keep", data-state="hide-menubar")
	h1 Studio
	h3 selected work
	hr
	code.url#exampleParameter .../demo-select.html

section(data-name="Identity", data-tag="branding")

	section.center
		h2 Identity

	section.center
		p Logo for “Harbour &amp; Fold”
		p.small A wordmark for a bindery. Drawn from the fold of a signature, which is the one shape every book on their shelves has in common.

	section.center
		p Logo for “Meridian Coffee”
		p.small A logo for Meridian Coffee Roasters. The logo is a cup seen from directly above.

section(data-name="Websites", data-tag="web")

	section.center
		h2 Websites

	section.center
		p “Harbour &amp; Fold”, online
		p.small A catalogue of about four hundred bindings, and a search that has to work when you only remember the colour.

	section.center
		p “Meridian Coffee”, online
		p.small A shop. Most of the work went into making the subscription page understandable in one screen.

section(data-name="Books", data-tag="print")

	section.center
		h2 Books

	section.center
		p “The Fold”, a monograph
		p.small 240 pages, two colours, sewn. The grid is built on the page proportion rather than on a column count.

section(data-name="Posters", data-tag="print")

	section.center
		h2 Posters

	section.center
		p A season of six
		p.small For a concert hall. One typeface, one rule, and a different colour per month.

section(data-name="About this demo", data-tag="keep")

	section.center
		h2 About this demo: “Select”
		p.small This is the #[i #[strong select]] demo: a presentation where a URL parameter picks which chapters or slides are shown, and every other marked section is hidden.

		p.small The bar along the top is #[a(href="https://github.com/martinomagnifico/reveal.js-simplemenu", target="_blank") Simplemenu]. Every one of these demos loads it, because it is the quickest way to see which chapters a parameter left standing.

	section.center
		h4 What you have been looking at
		p.small The portfolio above is all of the work, because you arrived without a parameter. Name a tag or a name in the URL and only those chapters are left — every other marked chapter is removed once the presentation starts.

	section
		h4 The markup
		p.small Selecting means the parameter picks what is shown. It can only choose between sections it can recognise, so everything it should be able to hide has to be marked. Each chapter here has a name and a tag.
		pre
			code.hljs.html(data-trim, data-line-numbers).
				&lt;section data-name="Identity" data-tag="branding"&gt; ... &lt;/section&gt;
				&lt;section data-name="Websites" data-tag="web"&gt;     ... &lt;/section&gt;
				&lt;section data-name="Books"    data-tag="print"&gt;   ... &lt;/section&gt;
				&lt;section data-name="Posters"  data-tag="print"&gt;   ... &lt;/section&gt;
		//-
		p.small The title slide and this chapter have #[code data-tag="keep"] instead, which leaves them out of the filters. They are shown whatever you include.

	section.center
		h4 The config
		p.small Nothing. Tags and names are in the markup, and #[code mode] is already #[code "select"] by default, so this deck configures nothing at all.
		p.small The one thing you would add is a group, which is next.

	section.center
		h4 Try it
		ul
			li #[a(href="?t=web") ?t=web] — the websites only
			li #[a(href="?t=print") ?t=print] — two chapters share that tag
			li #[a(href="?t=web,print") ?t=web,print] — either one
			li #[a(href="?n=identity") ?n=identity] — by name instead
			li #[a(href="demo-select.html") demo-select.html] — everything again

	section
		h4 A group
		p.small A group is a set of tags and/or names under one word, so the link can be short and you can change what it means later.
		pre
			code.hljs.js(data-line-numbers="3-5").
				tagteam: {
				    groups: {
				        pitch: {
				            tags: ["branding", "web"]
				        }
				    }
				}
		//-
		p.small #[a(href="?g=pitch") ?g=pitch] shows the identity work and the websites.

	section.center
		h4 Unhide, the other way round
		p.small Selecting makes the parameter #[em be] the presentation, so everything it should be able to hide has to be marked.
		p.small Unhiding is the opposite: only the extras are marked, and a parameter reveals them without touching anything else. See the #[a(href="demo-unhide.html") unhide demo].

section.center(data-tag="keep", data-state="hide-menubar")
	p Go to the #[a(href="demo.html") main demo]
